# Legacy Parity Standards

When replacing legacy functionality, identify the authoritative legacy implementation.

Trace legacy and modern implementations independently.

Compare:

- inputs;
- validation;
- defaults;
- null handling;
- branching;
- calculations;
- persistence effects;
- transaction behavior;
- errors;
- retries;
- duplicate behavior;
- ordering;
- external side effects.

Classify each material behavior as:

- MATCH
- DIFFERENCE
- UNKNOWN

For each difference determine whether it is:

- probable defect;
- intentional modernization;
- equivalent implementation difference;
- requires business clarification.

Do not require identical implementation structure.

Compare observable behavior.

Do not automatically reproduce apparent legacy defects.

Do not assume newer behavior is correct simply because it is newer.

Unknown behavior must be explicitly identified rather than invented.